    "created_at": "2018-04-20T20:23:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-20T20:23:45Z",
    "body": "As an additional data point, for our product having a unique identifier for pages that is easily accessible without jumping through hoops would be great.\r\n\r\nWe report latency/logging info from the service worker as well as the page. We log the client id in each, in order to link the data together either locally (by sending a message from the page to the SW), or on the server (by merging the two logs).\r\n\r\nWe're also experimenting with the WebLocksAPI OriginTrial (https://github.com/inexorabletash/web-locks), and it exposes a client id to identify the lock holder. We'd really like to be able to have a consistent identifier across these APIs, and it would be quite helpful if the ClientsAPI is also exposed from all contexts.\r\n\r\nIn some earlier, more hand written iteration of our locking system (before WebLocks), we had to use the SW Clients API to verify if the lock holder tab was still open. Pages needed to always talk to the SW to figure out their own id, and to find out whether another tab (by client id) was still open. Bringing all of this to the context of the page, would avoid adding extra complexity for cross-tab features.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
